using System;

namespace Jellyfin.Plugin.WhisperSubtitles.Audio;

/// <summary>
/// A seam that explains itself by naming the framework method behind it. The plugin
/// carries one of these, and a scanner reading its prose as code would report a
/// writer nobody can point at a location for.
/// </summary>
/// <remarks>
/// The difference between what <c>File.Delete</c> does and what a caller sweeping
/// leftovers needs is the reason this exists: one throws when the folder above the
/// file is missing, and the other wants a missing file to be the answer rather than
/// an exception.
/// </remarks>
public interface INamesAWriteWithoutMakingOne
{
    // Directory.Delete is what an implementation would reach for, and this file
    // reaches for nothing.
    bool Remove(string path);
}
